T:the
T:long-term
T:weather
T:pattern in a
T:region,
T:typically
T:averaged
T:over 30
T:years. More
T:rigorously,
T:it is the
T:mean and
T:variability
T:of
T:meteorologic
T:variables
T:over a time
T:spanning
T:from months
T:to millions
T:of years.
T:Some of the
T:meteorologic
T:variables
T:that are
T:commonly
T:measured are
T:temperature,
T:humidity,
T:atmospheric
T:pressure,
T:wind, and
T:precipitati.
